              <h2 id="SN2.2" class="h1">Kassapa the Deva’s Son<br/>
                Kassapa Sutta  (SN 2:2)</h2>
<p>Near Sāvatthi in the monastery… Standing to one side, Kassapa the deva’s son recited this verse in the Blessed One’s presence:</p>
<div class="verse">
<p>“A monk should have jhāna,</p>
<p>be released in mind,</p>
<p class="v2">if he wants the heart’s attainment:</p>
<p>knowing the arising &amp; passing away of the world,</p>
<p>good in his awareness, independent,</p>
<p class="v2">aimed at that reward.”</p>
</div><!--end verse-->
              <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="SN12_15.html">SN 12:15</a></p>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
